   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWd5r",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "Growing up in rural Hawke's Bay in a single-parent home in the 80s and 90s wasn't always easy. I recalls the impact of Ruth Richardson's 'mother of all budgets' on my family and the questions it raised for me about the sort of society he wanted to live in. I have always been interested in politics. I want to be part of a government, that will put people at the heart of its decision-making."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWd8g",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I have built a career fighting for the most vulnerable families in our communities, in uniform, in youth justice, and in mental health. I know what it means when the government cuts services, because I had to manage the consequences. I believe the partnership model can work successfully beyond social services, through centrally supported but locally delivered services and solutions for all New Zealanders."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWdBV",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Cost of iving is the biggest priority for this election. Everyone is doing it extremely tough."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWdEK",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Healthcare and access to healthcare, including GPs and the services at the hosptial."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWdH9",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Public transport options in parts of the electorate are woefully indaquate."
     }
    ],
