   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWcXz",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I got into politics because confidence in rural New Zealand was at an all-time low. It has improved, but there's much more to do. I want my daughters, if they choose farming, to have the freedom to farm well without the red tape I've faced for 20 years. I'm asking you to party vote ACT, so more ACT MPs can back rural NZ, grow the economy, defend equal rights, and restore consequences for crime."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWcao",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I'm not asking you to elect me as your local MP; I'm asking you to give your party vote to ACT to Lock Labour Out and Unlock New Zealand's potential. It means keeping the coalition Government in power, but ensuring that it can go further and faster on the issues that matter most to you. A party vote for ACT will re-elect the Government and make it stronger. I am a current ACT Government Minister."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWcdd",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Let farmers farm, cut red tape, protect property rights, crack down on rural crime, no new taxes."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWcgS",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Better services including rural school buses, police, and closing the medicines gap with Australia."
     },
     {
      "_key": "227mFCOl8uclHuS5roWcjH",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Make decisions based on need, not race, and with one law for all and one future together."
     }
    ],
